course: dictionary
lesson: 2060
title: What does conservation mean?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Conservation means looking after something carefully so it is not harmed, wasted or lost. The word is often used for nature, but it can also mean keeping old things safe. Look at the clue in this sentence: «Museums ask people not to touch art because oils and sweat from hands damage paint over time; conservation means keeping art safe for the future.» The sentence tells you what conservation means, so you do not even need a dictionary.
explain: Conservation can mean protecting wild animals, plants, forests and seas. «Modern zoos say they exist for conservation, education, research and helping people love animals.» Here conservation is one of the zoo's main jobs, and it means protecting animals and their homes.
explain: Conservation can also mean using things carefully so less is wasted. Words like «water conservation» and «energy conservation» show this. When you turn off a tap or a light you are helping with conservation.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If you put «keeping art safe» in place of «conservation», and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. In science, conservation can also mean a rule, such as «conservation of mass», which is a different meaning and is worked out from the context.
fact: Conservation means protecting nature so that animals, plants, forests and seas are not damaged or lost.
fact: «Water conservation» means using water carefully so that less is wasted.
fact: Conservation can also mean looking after old buildings, paintings and objects so they last a long time.
fact: In science, «conservation of mass» means that when ice melts or things mix, the total mass stays the same.
fact: «Conservation area» and «national park» are places where nature and old things are protected.
exercise: «Museums ask people not to touch art because oils and sweat from hands damage paint over time; conservation means keeping art safe for the future.» What does conservation mean here? | Painting over old pictures | *Keeping art safe so it lasts | Touching art to make it shine | Selling paintings to people
exercise: Mia says, «Let's do water conservation at home.» What is she asking everyone to do? | Throw away water that is still clean | Run the taps all day | *Use water carefully so less is wasted | Fill the bath to the very top
exercise: Find and copy the word from this sentence that means looking after nature and animals so they are not harmed: «Good zoos are accredited by associations such as the AZA in America, which check care, safety and conservation.» | associations | accredited | America | *conservation
test: «The USA has over 200 accredited zoos and aquariums, and they share breeding plans and fund conservation together.» What does conservation mean here? | Feeding the visitors | Closing zoos down | Spending money on new buildings only | *Protecting animals and nature, for example by helping them breed
test: In science, what does «conservation of mass» mean? | Mass always gets bigger when ice melts | Mass means how big a zoo is | *When ice melts or things mix, the total mass stays the same | Mass is a type of animal
exam: Which of these is NOT a meaning of conservation? | Protecting nature so it is not harmed | Using energy carefully so less is wasted | Looking after old paintings so they last | *Winning a race by running very fast
